   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "Union recipe recovered. Nitrogen is NH4Cl only at 0.75 mM (nitrate omitted, ASP-2-N base); N-deprivation in the paper is achieved by interrupting the chemostat feed. This record is the pure-Ar (no CO2) variant, so NO inorganic carbon/bicarbonate is supplied in the gas and there is no organic carbon in the defined medium; the sister condition uses 1.3% CO2-Ar. Trace-metal concentrations (Co/Zn ~exact, Mn within 30%) are consistent with PII metals dosed at ~0.1 mL/L into ASP-2. Vitamin B12 (cyanocobalamin) is present in many ASP/ES seawater media but is NOT specified for van Baalen's modified AS"
  },
